{"schema": "inflections@1", "language": "klingon", "notes": ["Written for this project. Every content word of the Klingon matrix column, with the forms its affix tables make.", "Verbs take a pronominal prefix for the subject: jI- (I), bI- (you), ma- (we), Su- (you all), and none for he, she, it or they. With a third-person object the prefix is vI- (I), Da- (you), wI- (we), bo- (you all), lu- (they) and none for he or she. Forms with an object carry @object. Objects in the first or second person (mu-, cho-, and so on) are not listed yet.", "Klingon has no tense. The suffix -pu' (perfective, done) is listed as @past; a verb with no aspect suffix is @present. Commands take yI- (to one person) and pe- (to several, no object).", "Nouns list the plural: -pu' for beings that speak (noun-speaker), -mey for other things (noun-thing). A mass noun (noun-mass) lists none. Places add -Daq (@place, in or at).", "Pronouns carry their person. Klingon usually drops a subject pronoun, because the verb's prefix says it.", "Negation (-be'), questions (-'a') and the topic (-'e') stay separate affixes in the matrix column; they are not listed per word."]}
